===Etymology 1===
Adverb from {{inh|en|enm|les|id=less}}, {{m|enm|lesse|id=less}}, {{m|enm|leasse}}, {{m|enm|lasse|id=less}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lǣs|t=smaller, less}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*laisiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leys-|t=to shrink, grow thin, be gentle}}.{{rfv-etym|en}} Cognate with {{cog|ofs|lēs|t=less}}, {{cog|osx|lēs|t=less}}. According to Kroonen (2013), from a northern Indo-European root {{der|en|ine-pro|*leh₂is-}} or ''*leh₃is-'', which he connects to {{cog|lt|liesas|t=lean}}.

Determiner and preposition from {{inh|en|enm|lees}}, {{m|enm|lesse}}, {{m|enm|leasse}}, {{m|enm|lasse}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lǣssa|t=less}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*laisizan-}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*laisiz|t=smaller, lesser, fewer, lower}} (see above). Cognate with {{cog|ofs|lessa|t=less}}.

Verb from {{inh|en|enm|lessen}}, from the determiner.

Noun from {{inh|en|enm|lesse}}, from the determiner.

